{"bug":"K001","report":"C","v":"found","ref":"3. Responses missing `:status` become successful responses","evidence":"“leaves `Response::builder()`’s default status when `:status` is absent” and “actual behavior is `200 OK`.” Identifies the client conversion accepting a missing status by retaining the default instead of returning a stream protocol error."}
{"bug":"K004","report":"A","v":"missed","ref":"1. Large capacity reservations silently become zero","evidence":"“`reserve_capacity(1usize << 32)` becomes a zero reservation.” This concerns reservation truncation, not release_capacity accepting more than the unreleased received bytes. No such over-release is identified elsewhere."}
{"bug":"K007","report":"C","v":"missed","ref":"4. Header lists exactly at the configured maximum are rejected","evidence":"“use `<` instead of `<=`.” This identifies rejection at a configured header-list boundary, not a HeaderMap::append panic from more than 24,576 unique fields under the default limit. That defect is absent throughout the report."}
